 "relocation_note": "The comparison with the baseline ignores running headers and page numbers. changed_pages lists every page that is not, word for word, a page of the baseline; it is the union of three lists. text_changed_pages (34) carry new or edited text: the abstract and contents (1 to 3); the introduction and the new overview with its status table (4, 6 to 11); a renumbered table caption in Section 8 (25); Sections 11 to 14, with pointers to the new results, the reworded opening of Section 12 and reworded status remarks (31 to 35, 37, 38); the new Section 14.8 (44 to 49); Sections 15 and 18 (50, 54 to 57, 62); and Appendices C, N, S and V, one sentence, word or table number each (79, 140, 159, 177). These are the pages on which the source changes of this build fall; core.tex and the other unchanged sources contribute none. reflowed_pages (34) have the baseline's text, apart from capitalized reference names, with page breaks moved by the insertions before them. reference_name_pages (26) each reproduce one baseline page and differ from it only in reference names that cleveref now capitalizes. relocated_pages maps each of the remaining 98 pages to the baseline page it reproduces, twelve pages earlier; their word boxes agree with the baseline's to within 0.01pt. The baseline is main at 5c27c46, whose v6 sources and status.json match the status-coverage-20261107 build record.",
 "layout_notes": [
  "All 94 changed pages of this exact build were rendered at 72 dpi and inspected, with pages 105 and 106, whose text extraction order differs from the baseline although their word boxes do not. No clipping, overlap, text in a margin, stranded heading or split display was seen. The title page holds the abstract and the whole provenance note; the grouped table of contents fills pages 2 and 3.",
  "Word boxes were also compared mechanically with the text block, whose edges are read from the running header, on every page. The only line that extends more than 3pt past the right edge is the inherited overfull line of Appendix C, on page 88 here and page 76 of the baseline, and no page sets text lower than the baseline's lowest line. The title page's last line is 33pt higher than in the baseline. The log has no warning other than that overfull line.",
  "The existing tables are renumbered from 1 to 3 to 4 to 6, because the overview adds three tables before them. Section, theorem and equation numbers are unchanged: the new statements take the numbers 14.9 to 14.15 after the last existing statement of Section 14, and the displays of Section 14.8 carry the tags (W1) to (W9)."
 ]
